    <item>
      <title>How to access shared folder in Linux guest in VirtualBox</title>
      <link>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2014-09-23-shared-folder/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 23 Sep 2014 11:22:48 +0800</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2014-09-23-shared-folder/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Make sure the VBOx extensions are installed.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Go here for details:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Add share&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;add-share&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#add-share&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In VirtualBox, Device add transient shared folder:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img&#xA;    class=&#34;my-0 rounded-md&#34;&#xA;    loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;    decoding=&#34;async&#34;&#xA;    fetchpriority=&#34;low&#34;&#xA;    alt=&#34;&#34;&#xA;    src=&#34;https://miroadamy.com/images/virt-box.png&#34;&#xA;    &gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This one has made available path /Users/Shared/ATG-11 under the name ATG-11&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Mount it&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;mount-it&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#mount-it&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight-wrapper&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;sudo mount -t vboxsf ATG-11 /media&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ ll /media/Unix/&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;total 19M&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;drwxr-xr-x. 1 root  408 Sep 12 16:02 ATG11-1&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;drwxr-xr-x. 1 root  272 Sep 12 16:02 ATG11-docs&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;-rw-rw-r--. 1 root  675 May 13 23:46 atg-platform-mac.userlibraries&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;-rw-rw-r--. 1 root  787 May 13 23:17 atg-platform-vm.userlibraries&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;-rwxr--r--. 1 root  19M Feb 15  2013 jrebel-5.1.3-nosetup.zip&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;-rw-r--r--. 1 root 1020 May 15 15:36 jrebel.lic&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;-rw-r--r--. 1 root  582 May 15 14:58 rebel.xml&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;drwxr-xr-x. 1 root  272 Apr  6 01:33 security&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;drwxr-xr-x. 1 root  306 Jun  9 22:34 servers&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;-rwxr--r--. 1 root  349 Dec 17  2013 users.txt&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;drwxr-xr-x. 1 root  340 Sep  3 16:10 xrebel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Installation of sshfs in the new VM</title>
      <link>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2014-03-11-sshf-in-vm/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 11 Mar 2014 11:22:48 +0800</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2014-03-11-sshf-in-vm/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Installation of sshfs in the new VM&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;installation-of-sshfs-in-the-new-vm&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#installation-of-sshfs-in-the-new-vm&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;On Centos 6, the fuse-sshfs is not part of default YUM repos.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Get the &amp;rsquo;epel&amp;rsquo; repos&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;get-the-epel-repos&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#get-the-epel-repos&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight-wrapper&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;wget http://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/6/x86_64/epel-release-6-8.noarch.rpm&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;wget http://rpms.famillecollet.com/enterprise/remi-release-6.rpm&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;sudo rpm -Uvh remi-release-6*.rpm epel-release-6*.rpm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Validate&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight-wrapper&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ ls -1 /etc/yum.repos.d/epel* /etc/yum.repos.d/remi.repo&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;/etc/yum.repos.d/epel.repo&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;/etc/yum.repos.d/epel-testing.repo&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;/etc/yum.repos.d/remi.repo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It if good idea to enable the remi by default&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>How to make screenshot from command line</title>
      <link>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2013-09-24-screenshot-cli/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 24 Sep 2013 11:22:48 +0800</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2013-09-24-screenshot-cli/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;How to make screenshot from command line&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;how-to-make-screenshot-from-command-line&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#how-to-make-screenshot-from-command-line&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight-wrapper&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;platform-edc $ screencapture -i ~/Desktop/$(date +%Y%m%d%H%M%S).png&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;libpng warning: zero length keyword&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;libpng warning: Empty language field in iTXt chunk&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt; &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;platform-edc $ screencapture  ~/Desktop/A$(date +%Y%m%d%H%M%S).png&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;libpng warning: zero length keyword&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;libpng warning: Empty language field in iTXt chunk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First one is &amp;ldquo;interactive&amp;rdquo; - Cmd-Shift-3 with selection tool, second is full screen&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Case sensitivity and VirtualBox shared folder</title>
      <link>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2013-09-16-vbox-shared-folder/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Sep 2013 11:22:48 +0800</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2013-09-16-vbox-shared-folder/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Case sensitivity and VirtualBox shared folder&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;case-sensitivity-and-virtualbox-shared-folder&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#case-sensitivity-and-virtualbox-shared-folder&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Weird but true behaviour:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have the case sensitive encrypted disk (sparse bundle with HFSX type) mounted in VBox shared folders. All works fine, after VM starts:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight-wrapper&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;touch zz zZ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;creates two files, both &amp;ldquo;inside VM&amp;rdquo; &lt;code&gt;~/development/ATG/platform-edc&lt;/code&gt; as well as in OS-X.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If the VM is suspended and resumed, it looses the case sensitivity inside the VM.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Usable mc color scheme</title>
      <link>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2013-09-05-mc-color-scheme/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 05 Sep 2013 21:32:48 +0800</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2013-09-05-mc-color-scheme/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Usable mc color scheme&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;usable-mc-color-scheme&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#usable-mc-color-scheme&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Edit&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;~/.mc/ini&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;insert&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight-wrapper&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;[Colors]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;base_color=lightgray,blue:normal=blue,default:selected=white,brightblue:marked=yellow,default:markselect=yellow,gray:directory=brightblue,default:executable=brightgreen,default:link=cyan,default:device=brightmagenta,default:special=lightgray,default:errors=red,default:reverse=green,default:gauge=green,default:input=white,gray:dnormal=green,gray:dfocus=brightgreen,gray:dhotnormal=cyan,gray:dhotfocus=brightcyan,gray:menu=green,default:menuhot=cyan,default:menusel=green,gray:menuhotsel=cyan,default:helpnormal=cyan,default:editnormal=green,default:editbold=blue,default:editmarked=gray,blue:stalelink=red,default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img&#xA;    class=&#34;my-0 rounded-md&#34;&#xA;    loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;    decoding=&#34;async&#34;&#xA;    fetchpriority=&#34;low&#34;&#xA;    alt=&#34;&#34;&#xA;    src=&#34;https://miroadamy.com/images/mc-color-scheme.png&#34;&#xA;    &gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>ATG Development using &#39;hidden&#39; VM</title>
      <link>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2013-04-22-atg-development/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 22 Apr 2013 11:22:48 +0800</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://miroadamy.com/posts/2013-04-22-atg-development/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Brief description of my latest setup I use for CPL and LCH - in case I forget it or somebody wants to replicate it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Inspiration for the setup came from &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_embedded&amp;amp;v=cPt_1Vga-Nk&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&gt;https://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_embedded&amp;v=cPt_1Vga-Nk&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Motivation - issues with VMs&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;motivation---issues-with-vms&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#motivation---issues-with-vms&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;VMs are great - they allow &amp;ldquo;packaged&amp;rdquo; dev environment and quick start for the new member of the team. Start a VM on local or remote host, connect with VNC or Remote Desktop and you are in business.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
